            <p class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-600 uppercase tracking-widest">Doc Ref: Interactive Study Guide & Data Analysis</p>
        </header>

        <!-- PART ONE: MULTIPLE CHOICE -->
        <section class="mb-16 relative z-10">
            <div class="border-b-2 border-slate-300 pb-2 mb-6 flex items-baseline justify-between">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Part One: Multiple-Choice</h2>
                <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-500 interactive-only">Auto-Grading Active</span>
            </div>
            
            <p class="text-slate-700 mb-8 italic">Read the scenarios and select the best answer. The system will verify your selection immediately.</p>

            <!-- Scenario 1: Hockey -->
            <div class="scenario-box bg-slate-100 border-l-4 border-slate-800 p-5 mb-6 shadow-[3px_3px_0px_rgba(203,213,225,1)] rounded-sm">
                <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-500 block mb-1">Scenario 01</span>
                <p class="m-0 text-slate-900">A local hockey player scored the following number of goals over their last 5 games: <strong>1, 2, 2, 4, 6</strong></p>
            </div>

            <div class="mb-8 pl-2">
                <p class="font-bold mb-3">1. The mean score was:</p>
                <div class="space-y-2 font-mono text-sm">
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q1" value="A" onclick="checkMCQ('q1', 'B')" class="mr-2"> A. 2</label>
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q1" value="B" onclick="checkMCQ('q1', 'B')" class="mr-2"> B. 3</label>
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q1" value="C" onclick="checkMCQ('q1', 'B')" class="mr-2"> C. 4</label>
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q1" value="D" onclick="checkMCQ('q1', 'B')" class="mr-2"> D. 5</label>
                </div>
                <div id="feedback-q1" class="mt-2 min-h-[24px]"></div>
            </div>

            <div class="mb-8 pl-2">
                <p class="font-bold mb-3">2. The mode was:</p>
                <div class="space-y-2 font-mono text-sm">
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q2" value="A" onclick="checkMCQ('q2', 'A')" class="mr-2"> A. 2</label>
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q2" value="B" onclick="checkMCQ('q2', 'A')" class="mr-2"> B. 3</label>
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q2" value="C" onclick="checkMCQ('q2', 'A')" class="mr-2"> C. 4</label>
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q2" value="D" onclick="checkMCQ('q2', 'A')" class="mr-2"> D. 5</label>
                </div>
                <div id="feedback-q2" class="mt-2 min-h-[24px]"></div>
            </div>

            <div class="mb-10 pl-2">
                <p class="font-bold mb-3">3. The median was:</p>
                <div class="space-y-2 font-mono text-sm">
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q3" value="A" onclick="checkMCQ('q3', 'A')" class="mr-2"> A. 2</label>
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q3" value="B" onclick="checkMCQ('q3', 'A')" class="mr-2"> B. 3</label>
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q3" value="C" onclick="checkMCQ('q3', 'A')" class="mr-2"> C. 4</label>
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q3" value="D" onclick="checkMCQ('q3', 'A')" class="mr-2"> D. 5</label>
                </div>
                <div id="feedback-q3" class="mt-2 min-h-[24px]"></div>
            </div>

            <!-- General Theory -->
            <div class="mb-8 pl-2">
                <p class="font-bold mb-3">4. When a researcher calculates a large standard deviation, the numbers in the data set are:</p>
                <div class="space-y-2 font-mono text-sm">
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q13" value="A" onclick="checkMCQ('q13', 'C')" class="mr-2"> A. very small values</label>
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q13" value="B" onclick="checkMCQ('q13', 'C')" class="mr-2"> B. clumped closely together</label>
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q13" value="C" onclick="checkMCQ('q13', 'C')" class="mr-2"> C. spread far apart</label>
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q13" value="D" onclick="checkMCQ('q13', 'C')" class="mr-2"> D. very large values</label>
                </div>
                <div id="feedback-q13" class="mt-2 min-h-[24px]"></div>
            </div>

            <div class="mb-8 pl-2">
                <p class="font-bold mb-3">5. Which of the following is a measure of variability?</p>
                <div class="space-y-2 font-mono text-sm">
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q14" value="A" onclick="checkMCQ('q14', 'A')" class="mr-2"> A. Range</label>
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q14" value="B" onclick="checkMCQ('q14', 'A')" class="mr-2"> B. Mean</label>
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q14" value="C" onclick="checkMCQ('q14', 'A')" class="mr-2"> C. Mode</label>
                    <label class="block cursor-pointer hover:bg-slate-200 p-2 rounded-sm transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-slate-300"><input type="radio" name="q14" value="D" onclick="checkMCQ('q14', 'A')" class="mr-2"> D. Distribution</label>
                </div>
                <div id="feedback-q14" class="mt-2 min-h-[24px]"></div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Page Break for Print -->
        <div class="page-break"></div>

        <!-- PART TWO: WRITTEN RESPONSES -->
        <section class="mb-16 relative z-10">
            <div class="border-b-2 border-slate-300 pb-2 mb-6 flex items-baseline justify-between mt-12 md:mt-0">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Part Two: Conceptual Analysis</h2>
                <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-500 interactive-only">Manual Entry</span>
            </div>
            
            <p class="text-slate-700 mb-8 italic">Draft your responses below. Use the tool to check your logic against psychological principles.</p>

            <div class="space-y-10">
                <!-- Q1 -->
                <div>
                    <label class="block font-bold mb-2">1. Is it possible to score in the 65th percentile yet not pass an exam? Explain.</label>
                    <textarea class="auto-expand w-full bg-slate-50 border border-slate-300 p-3 font-serif text-slate-800 focus:bg-white focus:border-slate-800 focus:ring-0 focus:outline-none rounded-none transition-colors shadow-[3px_3px_0px_rgba(203,213,225,0.6)] mb-3 min-h-[96px] overflow-hidden" placeholder="Enter your rationale..." oninput="this.style.height = ''; this.style.height = this.scrollHeight + 'px'"></textarea>
                    
                    <button onclick="toggleHint('hint1')" class="interactive-only font-mono text-xs border-2 border-slate-800 bg-white px-4 py-2 text-slate-900 font-bold uppercase tracking-wider shadow-[3px_3px_0px_rgba(30,41,59,1)] active:shadow-none active:translate-y-[3px] active:translate-x-[3px] transition-all">
                        Reveal Logic Check
                    </button>
                    <div id="hint1" class="hidden mt-4 bg-slate-100 border-l-4 border-slate-800 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-slate-700 shadow-[2px_2px_0px_rgba(203,213,225,1)]">
                        <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 uppercase tracking-widest text-xs block mb-1">System Hint</span>
                        Think about what a percentile actually measures. It compares you to *other people*, not to the raw score of the test itself. If everyone did poorly, doing better than 65% of people might still mean a failing raw score!
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Q2 -->
                <div>
                    <label class="block font-bold mb-2">2. Define reliability as it pertains to scientific experimentation and state why it is important.</label>
                    <textarea class="auto-expand w-full bg-slate-50 border border-slate-300 p-3 font-serif text-slate-800 focus:bg-white focus:border-slate-800 focus:ring-0 focus:outline-none rounded-none transition-colors shadow-[3px_3px_0px_rgba(203,213,225,0.6)] mb-3 min-h-[96px] overflow-hidden" placeholder="Enter your rationale..." oninput="this.style.height = ''; this.style.height = this.scrollHeight + 'px'"></textarea>
                    
                    <button onclick="toggleHint('hint2')" class="interactive-only font-mono text-xs border-2 border-slate-800 bg-white px-4 py-2 text-slate-900 font-bold uppercase tracking-wider shadow-[3px_3px_0px_rgba(30,41,59,1)] active:shadow-none active:translate-y-[3px] active:translate-x-[3px] transition-all">
                        Reveal Logic Check
                    </button>
                    <div id="hint2" class="hidden mt-4 bg-slate-100 border-l-4 border-slate-800 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-slate-700 shadow-[2px_2px_0px_rgba(203,213,225,1)]">
                        <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 uppercase tracking-widest text-xs block mb-1">System Hint</span>
                        Reliability is all about <em>consistency</em>. If you use a measuring tape to measure a board three times, you should get the exact same number three times. Without it, you can't trust your tools!
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Q3 -->
                <div>
                    <label class="block font-bold mb-2">3. Define negative feedback and provide an example of a system that uses it.</label>
                    <textarea class="auto-expand w-full bg-slate-50 border border-slate-300 p-3 font-serif text-slate-800 focus:bg-white focus:border-slate-800 focus:ring-0 focus:outline-none rounded-none transition-colors shadow-[3px_3px_0px_rgba(203,213,225,0.6)] mb-3 min-h-[96px] overflow-hidden" placeholder="Enter your rationale..." oninput="this.style.height = ''; this.style.height = this.scrollHeight + 'px'"></textarea>
                    
                    <button onclick="toggleHint('hint3')" class="interactive-only font-mono text-xs border-2 border-slate-800 bg-white px-4 py-2 text-slate-900 font-bold uppercase tracking-wider shadow-[3px_3px_0px_rgba(30,41,59,1)] active:shadow-none active:translate-y-[3px] active:translate-x-[3px] transition-all">
                        Reveal Logic Check
                    </button>
                    <div id="hint3" class="hidden mt-4 bg-slate-100 border-l-4 border-slate-800 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-slate-700 shadow-[2px_2px_0px_rgba(203,213,225,1)]">
                        <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 uppercase tracking-widest text-xs block mb-1">System Hint</span>
                        Negative feedback counteracts a change to bring a system back to a stable baseline (homeostasis). Think about cruise control in a car, or how your pupils react to bright light.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Page Break for Print -->
        <div class="page-break"></div>

        <!-- PART THREE: INTERACTIVE DATA CRUNCHER -->
        <section class="relative z-10">
            <div class="border-b-2 border-slate-300 pb-2 mb-6 flex items-baseline justify-between mt-12 md:mt-0">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Part Three: The Data Cruncher</h2>
                <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-700 interactive-only">Live Calc Active</span>
            </div>
            
            <p class="text-slate-700 mb-6 italic">Calculate the central tendencies and variability for the hand widths of 10 grade four students. Inputs will illuminate <span class="text-emerald-700 font-bold">green</span> upon exact verification.</p>
            
            <div class="data-cruncher-box bg-[#f0fdf4] border-2 border-emerald-900 p-6 md:p-8 shadow-[6px_6px_0px_rgba(6,78,59,1)] relative">
                
                <!-- Dataset Ribbon -->
                <div class="bg-emerald-900 text-white font-mono text-sm sm:text-lg text-center p-3 mb-8 tracking-widest shadow-inner relative -mx-2">
                    7<span class="text-emerald-400 text-xs">cm</span> &middot; 
                    11<span class="text-emerald-400 text-xs">cm</span> &middot; 
                    10<span class="text-emerald-400 text-xs">cm</span> &middot; 
                    8<span class="text-emerald-400 text-xs">cm</span> &middot; 
                    8<span class="text-emerald-400 text-xs">cm</span> &middot; 
                    7<span class="text-emerald-400 text-xs">cm</span> &middot; 
                    9<span class="text-emerald-400 text-xs">cm</span> &middot; 
                    12<span class="text-emerald-400 text-xs">cm</span> &middot; 
                    10<span class="text-emerald-400 text-xs">cm</span> &middot; 
                    8<span class="text-emerald-400 text-xs">cm</span>
                </div>

                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-y-6 gap-x-8">
                    
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-emerald-200 pb-3">
                        <div>
                            <span class="block font-bold text-slate-900">1. Mode:</span>
                            <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-800">Most frequent</span>
